<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Tisá–Děčínský Sněžník circuit — Tisá both walls and Děčínský Sněžník complete loop [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From Tisá rozc. Sněžník, pass St Anna to the wall ticket area. Complete the small-wall nature trail and big-wall lower labyrinth to Turistická chata. Follow red via Ostrov ponds and Pod Císařem, then green and nature-trail paths to Hraniční bouda. Take the red southern path onto Děčínský Sněžník and its tower courtyard. Follow the upper rim and green eastern rocky descent, then the village road west to hotel Sněžník. Return on cycle route 3017 to the chalet and complete the big-wall upper red rim past St Anna to the start. Both wall circuits and Sněžník are required; the loop is about 19 km and needs a full day. Height gain and time are approximate. Use existing circuits, steps and boardwalks without rock climbing, barriers, shortcuts or cave or mine entry. Expect exposed cliffs and a steep descent. Prefer dry, snow-free daylight and calm weather. Check forestry, landowner and nesting restrictions: 2026 nesting closures ending on 31 July do not guarantee later access. Postpone if any required leg is unavailable. Check wall tickets and tower opening; only the outdoor courtyard is part of the walk. Watch road traffic and cyclists, check transport and parking, and carry a map for changes between nature-trail, red, green and cycle-route guidance.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Source: https://api.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=14.021,50.774,14.115,50.809. Changes: ordered original-node slices from complete captured OSM walking ways; only duplicate shared junction nodes removed. Canonical display simplifies existing source vertices. No synthetic connectors, private map/guide coordinates or elevations. Two-dimensional planning geometry; not navigation-grade or legal permission.

